eTamil — authors and copyright holders
======================================

Copyright in eTamil is held entirely by one person. This file says who, and
records the names the commit history shows, so that "who wrote this" has a
single answer rather than four.

  Esan Maruff <esan@etamil.in>
      Author and sole copyright holder, 2026-present.
      Design, compiler, standard library, documentation and website.

      One person, two names, and each is used where it does its job:

        **Esan Maruff** is the name on GitHub (@Maruff), on every other
        account, in Cargo.toml, on etamil.in and throughout the commit history.
        It is what a reader sees and what he prefers to be addressed as, so it
        is the canonical name in .mailmap.

        **Mohammed Maruff** is the legal name and the name on the published
        research. Copyright is asserted in it — in NOTICE and in every source
        file header — because that is the name that has to hold up if the
        licence is ever enforced.

      An ORCID iD is the thing that ties both names, the papers, the thesis and
      this software to one persistent identity. It is free, and registering one
      is the single highest-value item still outstanding here.

      PhD Scholar, Department of Computer Applications, School of Computer
      Information and Mathematical Sciences, B.S. Abdur Rahman Crescent
      Institute of Science and Technology, Vandalur, Chennai.


NAMES IN THE COMMIT HISTORY

Four author strings appear across the history. `.mailmap` folds them into one,
so `git shortlog -sne` and GitHub's contributor graph show a single author
without any history being rewritten:

  Esan Maruff <bmaruff@gmail.com>                     the usual one
  Maruff <bmaruff@gmail.com>                          same person, short form
  YourGitHubUsername <YourEmail@example.com>          see below
  Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>                      Co-Authored-By trailers

The third is GitHub's placeholder git config, committed before `user.name` and
`user.email` were set on that machine. It covers three commits between
2026-08-17 and 2026-08-22 (`7092e6f`, `91fc5a1`, `273cea2`). They are the
author's own work and `.mailmap` records them as such.

The fourth is an AI assistant credited in `Co-Authored-By` trailers on commits
it helped write. It is a record of how the work was done, not a claim of
authorship or copyright: those commits were directed, reviewed and committed by
the author, and copyright in them is his.


CONTRIBUTIONS

None yet — every line is the author's. Contributors will be added here as they
arrive, and CONTRIBUTING.md sets out the Developer Certificate of Origin
sign-off that keeps this record accurate as that happens.

Copyright is not assigned to the project. A contributor keeps copyright in what
they wrote and licenses it under AGPL-3.0-or-later by signing off. That means
this file stops being a list of one person and becomes the list of everyone the
licence has to be honoured towards.
